  "id": "langerhans-cells",
  "term": "Langerhans cells",
  "definition": "Langerhans cells are CD207 (langerin)-expressing cells found on the ocular surface that increase in dry eye disease. In this source, they appear to help limit inflammation and protect corneal nerves, suggesting a neuroprotective and immune-regulating role.",
